.Dd November 7, 2026
.Dt SOFTWAREUPDATE 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm softwareupdate
.Nd install rmxOS updates onto the sealed base
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl l | -list
.Op Fl -no-scan
.Op Fl -product-types Ar types
.Nm
.Fl d | -download
.Op Ar label ...
.Nm
.Fl i | -install
.Ar label ... | Fl a | -all | Fl r | -recommended | Fl -os-only
.Op Fl R | -restart
.Op Fl -no-auto-confirm
.Nm
.Fl -history
.Op Fl -verbose
.Nm
.Fl -background
.Nm
.Fl -help
.Pp
Other tools:
.Nm
.Cm status | Fl -dump-state
.Nm
.Cm rollback
.Op Fl -restart
.Nm
.Cm confirm | cancel
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The sealed base is the ZFS dataset
.Ar pool Ns /base/ Ns Ar lineage
(default
.Cm main ) .
The running environment's origin identifies its current chain.
Each boot environment
.Ar pool Ns /ROOT/ Ns Ar snapshot
is a read-only clone of one of its snapshots.
An update is a
.Ql zfs send -i
stream from the base's newest snapshot, received into
.Ar pool Ns /base/ Ns Ar lineage
as it is; no dataset is ever promoted.
When no incremental starts at the chain head, the catalog's
.Cm full
stream is received into a new chain, preserving the running and fallback
environments and their origin snapshots.
An existing lineage gets a generation below
.Ar pool Ns /base/ Ns Ar lineage Ns / Ns Ar snapshot ;
a new lineage uses its canonical dataset directly.
.Pp
.Fl -install
reads the catalog, refuses with one line and receives nothing when the base
has changed since its newest snapshot
.Pq Ql written No not 0 ,
when the update starts from another GUID than that snapshot's, or when the
stream is truncated, does not match the catalog's sha256, or its own origin
GUID does not match.
It then receives the stream, clones the new snapshot
.Pq Cm mountpoint Ns =/ , Cm canmount Ns = Ns Cm noauto , Cm readonly Ns = Ns Cm on ,
records the running environment, received snapshot, time and label durably in
.Pa /private/var/db/rmxos/fallback .
Only then does it activate the clone for one boot
.Pq Ql bectl activate -t .
A staging failure undoes the record and label as well as the receive.
With
.Fl -restart
the system restarts.
.Pp
The boot check
.Pq Ql --boot-check , No run by Ar org.rmxos.softwareupdate.boot-check
confirms the new environment on its first boot once the uptime reaches
.Cm confirm_delay
and a good-boot check passes: the four Data datasets are mounted, the
ownership list below holds, and the base's
.Ql written
is 0.
It then refreshes the ESP's loader
.Pq see Sx ESP ,
sets the pool's
.Cm bootfs
to the new environment, clears the one-boot setting, writes the history row,
and applies retention.
The check waits without the operation lock:
.Cm status
shows the seconds left,
.Cm rollback
during the wait prevents the confirm, and a shutdown during the wait does not
confirm.
When a check fails nothing is confirmed: the state is
.Cm boot-check-failed ,
the failed checks are in the history and
.Cm status ,
and
.Cm bootfs
is untouched, so the next restart returns to the fallback.
A boot that does not reach the check boots the previous environment next.
The update is listed again as not confirmed.
Installing its label or using
.Fl a
stages the existing clone again if its origin GUID matches and its
.Cm written
is zero; otherwise the failed receive is undone and the stream is installed
again, without removing protected environments or snapshots.
With
.Fl -no-auto-confirm
the check waits for
.Cm confirm ,
which refreshes the ESP's loader too;
before the restart,
.Cm cancel
removes the staged environment and the received snapshot.
The boot check also asserts the ownership list
.Pa /System/Library/LaunchDaemons/org.rmxos.softwareupdate.ownership :
no service is both an enabled rc service and a loaded launchd job, and every
listed job is loaded.
.Pp
.Cm rollback
sets
.Cm bootfs
back to the fallback environment.
.Cm status
shows the installed label, the base snapshot and its GUID,
.Ql written
on the base (a nonzero value is reported as a sealed-base change), the boot
environment, the fallback, during the wait the seconds until the boot check,
a failed check's reasons, the Data datasets and the last history rows.
.Fl -history Fl -verbose
shows every history row, with the failed checks of a
.Cm boot-check-failed
row and the sha256s of an
.Cm esp-refreshed
row.
.Pp
Retention keeps the newest
.Cm retain
environments and the snapshots they use, never the running, fallback or
.Cm bootfs
one.
.Nm
never writes
.Pa /boot/loader.conf
or the ESP's
.Pa loader.env .
.Ss ESP
At confirm, before
.Cm bootfs
moves, the ESP's loader follows the new root's
.Pa /boot/loader.efi .
The ESP is the one mounted msdosfs file system, or else the one
.Cm efi
partition
.Pq Xr gpart 8 ,
mounted at a temporary directory for the confirm; without an ESP nothing is
written.
A partition listed under a GEOM label
.Pq Pa diskid/ ... , Pa gpt/ ...
as well as under its device name counts once.
The loader is
.Pa efi/freebsd/loader.efi ,
or else
.Pa efi/boot/bootx64.efi .
When its sha256 differs from the root's, the new loader is written to a
temporary file beside it, synced and checked against the root's sha256, the
old one is kept beside it with
.Pa .prev
appended
.Pq Pa loader.efi.prev ,
and the new one is renamed over it.
Two ESPs, or any failure, refuse the confirm with one line and leave
.Cm bootfs
and the ESP as they were.
No other ESP file is written.
.Pp
Install, confirm, cancel, rollback, downloads, background scans, catalog lists,
and the boot check hold an exclusive
.Xr flock 2
on
.Pa /private/var/db/rmxos/softwareupdate.lock .
A concurrent caller exits 1 with one line naming the holder's PID, except the
boot check: after
.Cm confirm_delay
it names the holder, waits for the lock and then reads the fallback record
again, so a
.Cm cancel
or
.Cm rollback
meanwhile still prevents the confirm.
The lock file remains; process exit releases the lock, including after a kill.
Status and history remain available while an operation runs.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -catalog Ar DIR | URL
Developer option: read
.Pa catalog.json
and its streams from a directory or URL.
.It Fl -no-scan
Use the last fetched catalog.
.It Fl -verbose , Fl -force , Fl -agree-to-license
Accepted;
.Fl -verbose
adds rmxOS's columns to
.Fl -history .
.El
.Pp
.Fl -fetch-full-installer ,
.Fl -list-full-installers ,
.Fl -install-rosetta ,
.Fl -stdinpass ,
.Fl -user
and
.Fl -safari-only
are refused with one line.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/defaults/softwareupdate.conf , Pa /etc/softwareupdate.conf
.Cm catalog_url ,
.Cm retain
(default 3),
.Cm confirm_delay
(seconds, 0 to 600, default 600).
.Cm confirm_delay
is accepted only when each file present is a regular file owned by root and
writable only by root.
.It Pa /private/var/db/rmxos/fallback , Pa /private/var/db/rmxos/history
The fallback record and the history.
.It Pa /private/var/db/rmxos/softwareupdate/
The last fetched catalog and downloaded streams.
.It Pa /private/var/db/rmxos/softwareupdate.lock
Operation lock and holder PID; file presence alone does not hold the lock.
.El
.Sh CATALOG
.Pa catalog.json
is
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{"format": "rmxos-catalog-v2", "updates": [{"label": "...", "build": "...",
 "snapshot": "...", "origin_guid": "...", "target_guid": "...",
 "stream": "....zfs", "sha256": "...", "size": N}]}
.Ed
.Pp
with GUIDs as decimal strings.
Optional
.Cm lineage
defaults to
.Cm main .
Optional
.Cm full
has the same fields as an update except for
.Cm origin_guid ;
its stream must have a zero origin GUID.
Unknown catalog fields are ignored.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 when an operation is refused or fails, 2 for invalid arguments.
